WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.112 --> 00:00:16.876
Tom knew his wanted to catch him in a lie so he said, "Ma'am, I was so hot

2
00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.597
today that I dumped water from the well on my head.

3
00:00:20.297 --> 00:00:22.218
See, my hair is still wet."

4
00:00:23.218 --> 00:00:25.999
Aunt Polly was annoyed that she had overlooked Tom's wet hair.

5
00:00:26.019 --> 00:00:30.580
"He skipped school again," she thought.

6
00:00:31.708 --> 00:00:37.431
She decided to use her secret weapon; before school each morning she sewed Tom's collar shut with thread.

7
00:00:38.392 --> 00:00:42.174
"Tom, show me your shirt collar," said Aunt Polly sternly.

8
00:00:43.294 --> 00:00:47.297
If he had taken off his shirt to go swimming, she would see the broken thread and know!

9
00:00:48.937 --> 00:00:52.579
Aunt Polly was really surprised because the collar was still sewn shut.

10
00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:57.202
"Tom, I'm sorry I suspected you of skipping school today.

11
00:00:58.062 --> 00:01:00.724
It appears that I was wrong," said Aunt Polly.

12
00:01:01.972 --> 00:01:03.833
Tom accepted her apology gracefully.

13
00:01:04.733 --> 00:01:10.174
He was just about to leave when Sid said, "Didn't you sew Tom's collar with white thread this

14
00:01:10.254 --> 00:01:12.535
morning? Look here."

15
00:01:13.315 --> 00:01:14.515
He pointed at Tom's shirt.

16
00:01:14.535 --> 00:01:17.876
"Tom's collar is sewn with black thread."

17
00:01:17.896 --> 00:01:25.898
"Why, yes, I did sew it with white thread today," said Aunt Polly thoughtfully, and then her face

18
00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:33.192
changed. It turned red, her glasses slipped to the tip of her nose, and she screamed, "Boy, that's

19
00:01:33.432 --> 00:01:37.214
it!" Tom turned to Sid and said menacingly.

20
00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:39.894
"I'll beat you good for that!"

21
00:01:40.275 --> 00:01:40.935
he growled.

22
00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:45.356
Not wanting to hear what his punishment would be, he ran out the door.

23
00:01:45.376 --> 00:01:49.577
"I'll have to punish him tomorrow," said Aunt Polly to herself.

24
00:01:49.597 --> 00:01:51.578
"I'll make him work.

25
00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.879
He hates work, but I've got to teach him a lesson."

26
00:01:56.679 --> 00:01:58.040
Tom sat down under a tree.

27
00:01:59.112 --> 00:02:03.254
In the fading light, he examined the two needles he kept under the front collar of his shirt.

28
00:02:04.375 --> 00:02:06.917
One needle had white thread and the other had black.

29
00:02:10.218 --> 00:02:15.101
"Aunt Polly never would have noticed the thread, if it hadn't been for Sid," moaned Tom.

30
00:02:15.121 --> 00:02:16.542
"Darn it.

31
00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:20.965
I bet she'll make me work tomorrow, and tomorrow is Saturday."

32
00:02:21.505 --> 00:02:22.886
Tom was in a foul mood.

33
00:02:23.766 --> 00:02:26.588
He spent the rest of the evening planning his revenge on Sid.

34
00:02:29.036 --> 00:02:32.339
The next day Tom stood on the sidewalk with a paint bucket and a brush.

35
00:02:33.459 --> 00:02:34.420
He looked at the fence.

36
00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:40.164
It was ninety feet long and nine feet high, and he had to spend his whole Saturday painting

37
00:02:40.225 --> 00:02:44.268
it. He dipped his brush into the bucket and painted the first plank.

38
00:02:44.928 --> 00:02:45.649
Then he stopped.

39
00:02:45.669 --> 00:02:48.130
"This will take forever."

40
00:02:50.092 --> 00:02:50.672
He sighed.

41
00:02:52.394 --> 00:02:55.176
Suddenly Tom saw his friend Ben coming down the street.

42
00:02:56.192 --> 00:02:59.834
Tom picked up the brush and began painting again because he had a plan.

43
00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:01.914
Ben walked up to Tom.

44
00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:03.755
"Working, huh?

45
00:03:04.615 --> 00:03:05.556
I'm going swimming.

46
00:03:06.016 --> 00:03:07.196
Don't you wish you could come?"

47
00:03:08.677 --> 00:03:10.758
"I'm not working," replied Tom.

48
00:03:10.778 --> 00:03:13.459
"Yes, you are," said Ben.

49
00:03:13.479 --> 00:03:17.921
"Well, maybe it is working, but I like it," said Tom.

50
00:03:17.941 --> 00:03:21.162
"What?" shouted Ben.

51
00:03:21.182 --> 00:03:23.043
"You like it?"

52
00:03:23.943 --> 00:03:28.538
Tom kept painting, and said, "Boys don't get to paint a fence every day."

53
00:03:30.059 --> 00:03:31.841
Ben watched Tom paint for a while.

54
00:03:32.661 --> 00:03:34.163
The fence looked clean and white.

55
00:03:35.304 --> 00:03:40.067
Ben watched some more, and soon he started to think, "Painting looks easy.

56
00:03:41.028 --> 00:03:42.069
Painting looks fun."

57
00:03:44.231 --> 00:03:46.593
Before long Ben really wanted to paint too!

58
00:03:46.613 --> 00:03:49.815
"Let me try," he begged Tom.

59
00:03:49.835 --> 00:03:52.738
"No," said Tom.

60
00:03:52.758 --> 00:03:55.540
"Aunt Polly told me to do it.

61
00:03:56.604 --> 00:03:57.905
She said it was important.

62
00:03:58.726 --> 00:04:00.487
This is the street side of the fence.

63
00:04:01.248 --> 00:04:05.351
Only one boy in a thousand has the talent to paint the street side."

64
00:04:06.152 --> 00:04:08.594
Tom paused and pretended to think for a moment.

65
00:04:09.154 --> 00:04:12.777
"Maybe you can do the back side," he said.

66
00:04:12.797 --> 00:04:17.321
"I'll let you have my apple," Ben offered.

67
00:04:18.382 --> 00:04:20.924
Tom looked at Ben, and then he looked at the apple.

68
00:04:21.564 --> 00:04:22.725
He handed Ben the brush.

69
00:04:23.706 --> 00:04:26.048
While Ben painted, Tom rested in the shade.

70
00:04:27.136 --> 00:04:28.576
He ate the apple and smiled.

71
00:04:29.297 --> 00:04:30.337
His plan had worked.

72
00:04:32.217 --> 00:04:34.218
Soon other boys came and asked to paint too.

73
00:04:35.098 --> 00:04:40.440
By early afternoon both sides of the fence were finished, and Tom's pockets were full of presents.

74
00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:43.240
"May I play now?"

75
00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:44.621
Tom called to his aunt.

76
00:04:44.641 --> 00:04:47.301
"You can't be finished already!

77
00:04:47.802 --> 00:04:49.402
How much of the fence have you painted?"

78
00:04:49.842 --> 00:04:50.422
she asked.

79
00:04:50.442 --> 00:04:52.143
"All of it.

80
00:04:52.523 --> 00:04:54.203
Come and see," said Tom.

81
00:04:54.223 --> 00:04:58.105
"Don't you lie to me—," began Aunt Polly.

82
00:04:58.866 --> 00:05:01.270
Just then she spotted the freshly painted fence.

83
00:05:02.231 --> 00:05:06.576
She was so pleased with its clean appearance, she gave Tom a shiny red apple.

84
00:05:07.377 --> 00:05:08.960
Then she sent him off to play.
